  "regressions": 2,
  "scope": "Whole Federer 3.2.31, pp. 268\u2013269: the actual non-strict positive fibre threshold is Hausdorff measurable and finite measure rectifiable for every natural 0<=mu<=m, an H^m-measurable finite (H^m,m)-rectifiable original partial domain and a Lipschitz map on exactly that domain. All source/target ambient dimensions, zero dimensions and zero Lipschitz bounds are retained; individual fibres may have infinite mass.",
  "proof_route": "Independent small symmetric-majorant, projection-scale and compact null-overlap cover laws precede proved local existence. Actual range projections, eigenbases and exterior operator norms give the small rescaling. Closed C1 agreement pieces, actual differential agreement and local unit Lipschitz neighborhoods discharge measurability and cover summation. Finite dominated integral transport, the actual 3.2.30 distortion and rough 2.10.25 estimate give the printed coefficient; exact source-mass additivity removes epsilon without a cover-size factor. Critical-fibre nullity, 3.2.14/21, actual 3.2.18 compact charts and exact partial-graph transport finish the theorem.",
  "whole_original_partial_domain": true,
  "all_natural_degrees": true,
  "zero_source_and_target_dimensions": true,
  "zero_lipschitz_bounds": true,
  "non_strict_positive_threshold": true,
